    {
      "calls": [
        {
          "ID": "toolu_01CE4oxcNvi8uCjq4bNT6YYL",
          "Name": "submit_read",
          "Input": {
            "assessments": [
              {
                "facts": [
                  "F79",
                  "F80",
                  "F89",
                  "F81",
                  "F59",
                  "S16:F86",
                  "S16:F93",
                  "S11:F58",
                  "S10:F50"
                ],
                "ref": "N1",
                "statement": "The domestic announcements of the week read as one programme: a Prime Minister in office only since July is carrying his Greater Manchester mayoral model (devolved, localised employment support, public control of transport, regional presence) into national government, through DWP devolution, Number 10 North, a £2.5bn youth employment package and a Derby-based Great British Railways.",
                "supersedes": ""
              },
              {
                "facts": [
                  "S1:F12",
                  "S1:F13",
                  "S2:F33",
                  "S2:F34",
                  "S2:F40",
                  "S3:F16",
                  "S3:F38"
                ],
                "ref": "N2",
                "statement": "As the Record stands, the reciprocal energy ceasefire is still an announcement with no confirmed start date, and UK policy is built not to depend on it: London is speeding up air defence deliveries and widening sanctions on Russian oil and LNG at the same time.",
                "supersedes": ""
              },
              {
                "facts": [
                  "S16:F71",
                  "S16:F72",
                  "S16:F73",
                  "S16:F92",
                  "S17:F82",
                  "S16:F83",
                  "S20:F91"
                ],
                "ref": "N3",
                "statement": "The Scotland offer so far consists mostly of invitations and not agreements: the only joint commitment with money attached is the Scottish Government matching £10m for two defence technical colleges, so the first real test is the National Economic Council meeting with the devolved First Ministers, expected in late October or early November.",
                "supersedes": ""
              }
            ],
            "statements": [
              {
                "cites": [
                  "F80",
                  "F79",
                  "F74"
                ],
                "text": "The thread running through this week is a Prime Minister who is still new. He walked into Downing Street in July after leaving Westminster in 2017 to become Greater Manchester's first mayor, and he told the First Minister in his first week that he wanted to work with him."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "F89",
                  "F81",
                  "S16:F86",
                  "S16:F93"
                ],
                "text": "Much of what he announced in Scotland comes from his time as mayor. Having put Greater Manchester's buses back under public control and built its Live Well model, he now offers Scotland DWP devolution, a localised model of employment support, and has set up Number 10 North."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "F59",
                  "S10:F50",
                  "S11:F51",
                  "S11:F58",
                  "S14:F56"
                ],
                "text": "The rail announcements fit the same pattern. He fronted the unveiling of Great British Railways' headquarters in Derby, where 600 young apprentices are to enrol under a £2.5bn youth employment package and Alstom is to build £1bn of new trains for the north."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "N1"
                ],
                "text": "Taken together, this is less a set of separate initiatives than the mayoral approach being scaled up to national level, and it is worth reading future domestic announcements that way."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S16:F72",
                  "S16:F92",
                  "S17:F82",
                  "S16:F83",
                  "N3"
                ],
                "text": "Holyrood's response is less settled than the Briefings' tone suggests. The offer is described as serious and genuine, but the only joint money so far is Scotland matching £10m for two defence technical colleges. The test is the National Economic Council meeting with the First Ministers, due within a couple of weeks of 16 October."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S1:F12",
                  "S1:F13",
                  "N2"
                ],
                "text": "Abroad, the energy ceasefire is still only an announcement. Ukraine says it will comply as soon as a start date is confirmed, and the Record holds no confirmation of one."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S2:F34",
                  "S2:F40",
                  "S3:F16",
                  "S3:F38",
                  "S2:F33"
                ],
                "text": "London is not waiting for it. It is speeding up £10m of a £45m air-defence missile package, has sanctions covering over 90% of Russia's oil-producing capacity, plans a full maritime services ban on Russian LNG, and has asked ministers for more sanctions, military aid and fiscal packages."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S8:F27",
                  "S8:F85"
                ],
                "text": "The next fixed date is the UK-EU summit in Brussels on 20 November. The Prime Minister used his Scotland speech to say he will seek a new food and farming deal there, which ties the domestic agenda to the European one."
              }
            ],
            "stories": [
              {
                "developments": [
                  "S16:F93",
                  "S16:F86",
                  "S10:F50",
                  "S11:F58"
                ],
                "title": "The Burnham premiership: the mayoral model in national government"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
